      "• **Risk Awareness & Mitigation**: Good. Implicitly addresses technical and adoption risks through detailed planning (pilot, test ledger, witness consortium) and a privacy-first design that doesn't store raw data. The focus on a limited initial scope (specific standards, a pilot use case) shows an understanding of execution risk."
